---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import RelatedArticles from '../components/shared/RelatedArticles.astro';
import MidContentAd from '../components/shared/MidContentAd.astro';
import EndOfContentAd from '../components/shared/EndOfContentAd.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/shared/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import EditorialStandards from '../components/shared/EditorialStandards.astro';

const SITE = 'https://vitamindcalculator.net';
const PAGE_URL = `${SITE}/vitamin-d-and-metformin`;

const medicalJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'MedicalWebPage',
  name: 'Vitamin D and Metformin',
  url: PAGE_URL,
  medicalAudience: { '@type': 'MedicalAudience', audienceType: 'Patient' },
  lastReviewed: '2026-05-01',
};
const breadcrumbJsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: SITE },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Metformin', item: PAGE_URL },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Vitamin D and Metformin: B12 Depletion, Diabetes Care, and Combined Dosing"
  description="Metformin depletes B12; vitamin D is often paired with metformin for prediabetes and PCOS. What to monitor and how they fit together."
  ogType="article"
>
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(medicalJsonLd)} />
  <script slot="head" type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbJsonLd)} />

  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ href: "/vitamin-d-and-metformin", label: "Metformin" }]} />
  <EditorialStandards />

  <main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">Vitamin D and Metformin</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-8">
      Metformin is the most-prescribed diabetes drug worldwide. It's often
      combined with vitamin D supplementation — both are cheap, safe, and
      addressed together in prediabetes, T2D, and PCOS care. The key
      interaction to know: metformin depletes vitamin B12.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">B12 depletion — the well-established interaction</h2>
    <MidContentAd />
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      Chronic metformin use (~4+ years) reduces serum B12 by ~10-30% in
      long-term users. Prevalence of B12 deficiency in metformin users:
      5-10% overall, higher in older adults. American Diabetes Association
      recommends periodic B12 screening in long-term metformin users. This
      is not a vitamin D issue but is worth knowing. See our
      <a href="/vitamin-b12" class="text-amber-700 underline">B12 page</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Vitamin D and metformin combined</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
      No direct pharmacological interaction. Vitamin D + metformin combinations
      are common in:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>PCOS — vitamin D deficiency is common; metformin is standard care.</li>
      <li>Prediabetes — D2d trial tested vitamin D for T2D prevention; metformin is DPP evidence-based.</li>
      <li>T2D — vitamin D correction alongside standard diabetes care.</li>
      <li>Gestational diabetes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Practical care</h2>
    <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed space-y-2">
      <li>Long-term metformin users: check B12 every 2 years; more often if elderly, neuropathy, or anaemia.</li>
      <li>Vitamin D 1,000-2,000 IU/day standard dosing; correct any deficiency.</li>
      <li>Some patients benefit from a B12 supplement (500-1,000 µg oral cyanocobalamin) alongside metformin.</li>
      <li>The evidence-based diabetes prevention/treatment is metformin (or GLP-1 agonists, SGLT2 inhibitors) plus lifestyle change — vitamin D is adjunctive.</li>
    </ol>

    <EndOfContentAd />

    <div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-200 rounded-xl p-4 text-sm text-blue-900 mt-8 leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Not medical advice.</strong> Metformin has excellent long-term
      safety and effectiveness — the B12 issue is manageable with periodic
      monitoring.
    </div>

    <RelatedArticles current="/vitamin-d-and-metformin" />
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
